{
  "about": "A Number column's one number line (ADR-0023). C#'s reference implementation holds every number as a decimal, so a double reads at fifteen significant digits and at most 28 decimal places; the Script Core reads a number the same way and keeps a bigint exact, as C# keeps a long. A JSON number is a double in C# and a number in the Script Core; {\"bigint\": text} a long and a bigint; {\"double\": \"NaN\"} a value JSON cannot hold.",
